<%# Sticky contextual header for inner screens — debate, profile, dashboard, search
    (Hoojah 2026, redesign Phase 0, Task 0.3). Distinct from the global `shared/_navbar`,
    which stays fixed on every page; this partial is opt-in per screen and scrolls with
    the page until it hits the top, then sticks.

    Locals (plain partial, no strict locals — `action:` is free-form caller HTML, which a
    strict signature would fight):
      title:  required. Plain text, rendered as the screen's <h1>.
      back:   optional. A path/URL for a back link (lucide `arrow-left`). Nil or omitted
              renders no back link — `local_assigns.fetch(:back, nil)` so a caller that
              never mentions `back:` behaves identically to one that passes `back: nil`.
      action: optional. An html-safe string rendered in a right-hand slot (a button, a
              menu, a link) — never plain text, since it is inserted as markup.
%><% back = local_assigns.fetch(:back, nil) %>
<header class="sticky top-0 z-20 bg-nav backdrop-blur border-b border-hairline">
  <div class="max-w-xl mx-auto px-4 h-14 flex items-center gap-2">
    <% if back.present? %>
      <%# ~40px hit box, matching the navbar's tap targets. %>
      <%= link_to back, class: "flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 -ml-2 shrink-0 text-ink no-underline", aria: {label: "Back"} do %>
        <%= lucide_icon("arrow-left", class: "w-5 h-5") %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>

    <h1 class="flex-1 min-w-0 truncate text-base font-bold text-ink"><%= local_assigns[:title] %></h1>

    <% if local_assigns[:action].present? %>
      <div class="flex items-center shrink-0"><%= local_assigns[:action] %></div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</header>
